 "note": "Client side, appendix §F reply rule (t = fake monotonic clock, ms). The lease on an admitting receipt never restores control that was lost while the reply was in flight. (1) Local input revoked the lease (epoch 2) before the receipt naming epoch 1 arrived: lower than an epoch seen since the Send, dropped. (2) A takeover by another controller (epoch 4) beat the receipt naming epoch 3: dropped. (3) The attachment was replaced (a second hello, new welcome) before the receipt of a Send sent on the old one arrived: not outstanding on the current attachment, dropped. (4) The receipt of a Send sent at t=3000 arrives at t=18000: deadline = 3000 + 15000 = now, so control stays off (expiry is now >= deadline). A timely receipt (sent at 20000, applied at 20100) gives control until 20000 + 15000 = 35000. On one ordered link the host sends the receipt before such a lease_changed; these orders arise between Astation's own layers (native or API callers behind one attachment), and the client must hold either way."
}
